  {
   "slug": "speech-825291",
   "speaker": "Mitch Fifield",
   "party": "Liberal",
   "state": "federal",
   "date": "2013-06-27",
   "stage_hint": null,
   "brief": "The Coalition opposed the Charities Bill 2013, warning it could create legal disputes and burden charities, while the Greens supported it after securing clarifications that protect advocacy and environmental purposes. The government argued the bill modernises charity law, reduces red tape, and establishes a single regulatory \"passport\" for the sector."
